 "duration": 35.68,
 "text": "Mars has a moon that is falling.  Slowly.  Phobos drops about six feet closer to Mars every hundred years.  In 50 million years, it either crashes into Mars or shatters into a ring.  And on Monday, Japan launches a mission to go grab a piece of it.  It is called MMX. Land on Phobos, scoop up a sample, fly it home.  No mission has ever brought back a sample from Mars or its moons.  Why bother?  Because nobody knows where these moons came from.  That sample could finally tell us.  Liftoff is Monday on Japan's H-3 rocket.  Follow and we will show you the launch.",
